        "suggested_fix": "Use the same property name consistently across the dataset and the logic. Update the filter to reference `b.title` (or update the data to include a `name` field). Also ensure `query` is defined and trimmed before use.",
        "code_fix": "function renderBooks() {\n  const query = document.getElementById(\"search\").value.trim().toLowerCase();\n  const genre = document.getElementById(\"genre\").value;\n  const sort = document.getElementById(\"sort\").value;\n  let list = BOOKS.filter(b =>\n    (genre === \"all\" || b.genre === genre) &&\n    (query === \"\" || b.title.toLowerCase().includes(query) || b.author.toLowerCase().includes(query))\n  );\n  if (sort === \"price-asc\") list.sort((a, b) => a.price - b.price);\n  if (sort === \"price-desc\") list.sort((a, b) => b.price - a.price);\n  if (sort === \"title\") list.sort((a, b) => a.title.localeCompare(b.title));\n  /* render the list... */\n}",
